## Local development

```bash
npx wrangler d1 execute practiceroom --local --file=./schema.sql
npx wrangler dev --local
```

Without `RESEND_API_KEY` set, sign-in codes are printed to the Worker log instead
of emailed, so you can sign in locally without sending real mail.

Put local secrets in `.dev.vars` (already in `.gitignore` — **keep it there**):

```
AI_API_KEY=...
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=price_...
```

---

## If something breaks

**`not_signed_in` when signed in.** The session cookie is `SameSite=None; Secure`
because the site and API are on different hosts. It needs HTTPS on both ends, and
the browser must not be blocking third-party cookies. If you later put the API on
a subdomain of your own domain, you can relax this to `SameSite=Lax`.

**CORS errors.** `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in `wrangler.toml` must exactly match the site
origin — no trailing slash. Add your custom domain when you have one.

**Stripe webhook returns 400.** Almost always the wrong signing secret — test and
live endpoints have different ones. Stripe's dashboard shows the response body.

**The plan doesn't update after payment.** Check the webhook's delivery log in
Stripe. If deliveries are failing, the plan will never change, because Checkout
succeeding and your database knowing about it are two separate things.
